Part 3. Mixed profiles on a grid (2x2), step 1/400, thresholds lowered by the grid tolerance
Exact, prisoner's dilemma (5,3,1,0): u_1(p,q) = 1 - p + 4q - pq (p, q = probabilities of C). Round 1: m = (1,1).
  The section of p in E_1 is q in [p/(4-p), 4p/(1+p)]; u_1 increases in q, so its infimum is u_1(p, p/(4-p)) = 1
  for every p: m stays (1,1) and E_1 = {u_1 >= 1, u_2 >= 1} is the limit. It contains (D,D) and (C,C).
  check p=0: q=0.0000, u_1 = 1.000000, q <= 4p/(1+p): True
  check p=0.25: q=0.0667, u_1 = 1.000000, q <= 4p/(1+p): True
  check p=0.5: q=0.1429, u_1 = 1.000000, q <= 4p/(1+p): True
  check p=1: q=0.3333, u_1 = 1.000000, q <= 4p/(1+p): True
