Part 4. Correlated profiles, chicken, round 2: player 1 committing to C faces the distributions on row C with u_2 >= 1 (round-1 threshold), i.e. mu(CB) * 1 >= 1, so mu = CB and u_1 = 3 = her largest payoff; by symmetry m = (3,3), while u_1 + u_2 <= 4 at every distribution: no correlated profile survives.
   chicken: largest u_1 + u_2 over profiles 4.0
